# 高频词汇 List08
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2023恋练有词
# 描述: 高频词汇List08核心词汇

{{virtual}}{/ˈvɜːtʃuəl/}{虚拟的；实质的}{Online shopping has become virtually universal.}}
{{visible}}{/ˈvɪzəbl/}{可见的；明显的}{The results of the experiment were clearly visible.}}
{{vital}}{/ˈvaɪtl/}{至关重要的；生命的}{Water is vital for human survival.}}
{{volume}}{/ˈvɒljuːm/}{音量；体积；卷}{The volume of traffic has increased significantly.}}
{{voluntary}}{/ˈvɒləntri/}{自愿的；志愿的}{Participation in the survey is entirely voluntary.}}
{{welfare}}{/ˈwelfeər/}{福利；幸福}{The government should prioritize public welfare.}}
{{widespread}}{/ˈwaɪdspred/}{广泛的；普遍的}{There is widespread support for the new policy.}}
{{witness}}{/ˈwɪtnəs/}{目击；见证}{She witnessed the accident from her apartment window.}}
{{yield}}{/jiːld/}{产出；屈服}{The investment yielded impressive returns.}}
{{acknowledge}}{/əkˈnɒlɪdʒ/}{承认；致谢}{He acknowledged that he had made a mistake.}}
{{acquire}}{/əˈkwaɪər/}{获得；收购}{The company acquired a smaller competitor.}}
{{adapt}}{/əˈdæpt/}{适应；改编}{Animals must adapt to changing environments.}}
{{adequate}}{/ˈædɪkwət/}{足够的；适当的}{The facilities are adequate for our needs.}}
{{advocate}}{/ˈædvəkeɪt/}{提倡；倡导者}{She advocates for equal rights for all citizens.}}
{{allocate}}{/ˈæləkeɪt/}{分配；拨出}{The budget allocates funds for research and development.}}
{{alter}}{/ˈɔːltər/}{改变；修改}{The plan was altered to accommodate new requirements.}}
{{ambiguous}}{/æmˈbɪɡjuəs/}{模棱两可的；含糊的}{The instructions were ambiguous and led to confusion.}}
{{analyse}}{/ˈænəlaɪz/}{分析；解析}{Scientists analysed the data from the experiment.}}
{{anticipate}}{/ænˈtɪsɪpeɪt/}{预期；预料}{We anticipate a surge in demand during the holiday season.}}
{{apparent}}{/əˈpærənt/}{明显的；表面上的}{The solution was apparent from the beginning.}}
{{appreciate}}{/əˈpriːʃieɪt/}{感激；欣赏}{I appreciate your help with this project.}}
{{approach}}{/əˈprəʊtʃ/}{方法；接近}{We need a new approach to solve this problem.}}
{{appropriate}}{/əˈprəʊpriət/}{适当的；恰当的}{Please wear appropriate clothing for the occasion.}}
{{arise}}{/əˈraɪz/}{出现；产生}{Problems may arise during the implementation phase.}}
{{assert}}{/əˈsɜːt/}{断言；主张}{The author asserts that education is the key to success.}}
{{assess}}{/əˈses/}{评估；评定}{The teacher assessed each student's performance.}}
{{assign}}{/əˈsaɪn/}{分配；指派}{The manager assigned tasks to each team member.}}
{{associate}}{/əˈsəʊʃieɪt/}{联想；联合}{People often associate the color red with passion.}}
{{assume}}{/əˈsjuːm/}{假设；承担}{We cannot assume that everyone agrees with this plan.}}
{{assure}}{/əˈʃʊər/}{保证；使确信}{I assure you that the product is safe to use.}}
